### Template


### LOCAL SETUP
To run this locally, there are two options
1. running on docker (easiest and quickest)
2. running app with **HOT RELOAD**

#### Running on Docker
This is the fastest way to get up and running because this process will handle running the app with hot reload, running migrations on file change and any other necessary bootstrapping. Use docker compose by running 

```bash
    docker-compose -f docker-compose.[environment].yml build --build-arg TAG=$TAG
```

#### Starting App Manually With Hot Reload
To start the app locally with **hot reload**, run the following commands

```bash
    go install github.com/air-verse/air@latest

    air
```
> **NOTE** Ensure that your Go Path is synced with the bin directory of your local machine

#### Running The App By Yourself 
To run the app your self, ensure a `.env` file exists in the base directory, lookup the [.env.example file](./.env.example) for setup example. Afterwards run the command below
```bash
    go run ./
```

#### Running In Production
To have the app ready for production, run the following commands

```bash
    # Build executable
    go build -o ./tmp/main .

    # Make build executable
    chmod +x ./tmp/main

    ## Run the app
    ./tmp/main

```

